I agree that letting wizrds become wombats and vice versa would be a Bad Thing.
But I'm not sure that your argument stands up: it's quite hard to visualise a
nethack wizard as 'some geezer in his/her ninties, barely able to totter
through the dungeon, having studied arcane knowledge all his/her life,' when
they start off knowing only two spells. I'd rather take the view that your
class is your mindset / ambition / career path, and that if you start as a
wizard then you intend to end up as the pointy hatted spell slinger and aren't
going to change your plan half way.

